UPDATE "families" SET "name" = 'G Series Counterbalance Forklifts', "summary" = 'BYD''s G series of 1.6–5.0 t electric counterbalance forklifts, from compact trucks for tight aisles to 5-tonne trucks for heavier loads.', "how_it_works" = 'An **electric counterbalance forklift** lifts loads on forks at the front and balances them with the mass of the chassis, counterweight and battery at the rear. It is the general-purpose forklift. With a wheel at each corner and a wider footprint than a three-wheel truck, it is steadier on ramps, outdoor yards and long runs.

**Powertrain.** An 80 V lithium iron phosphate (LFP) battery supplies AC motor controllers. On BYD''s G series trucks, "B/C" variants use two traction motors on the front drive axle, while "D/E" variants use a single drive motor. The rear wheels steer through a hydraulic or electric power-steering system. Lifting is handled by its own AC motor driving a hydraulic gear pump.

**Hydraulics and mast.** A multi-spool valve sends pump oil to the lift cylinders, the tilt cylinders and any auxiliary functions, such as a side-shift or fork positioner. Two-stage (duplex) masts suit most loading work. Three-stage (triplex) full-free-lift masts reach higher racking while staying low enough to enter containers.

**Regeneration.** When the truck slows or lowers a load, its traction motors act as generators and feed energy back to the battery. This extends running time and saves brake linings.

**Battery, BMS and charging.** The BMS balances cells, monitors temperature and current, and talks to the matched charger. Because LFP tolerates partial charging, the truck can be topped up during breaks and shift changes rather than having its battery swapped.

**Load centre and stability.** Capacity is rated at a set load centre, usually 500 mm on these models. Moving the load''s centre further from the fork face, lifting higher or tilting forward reduces the safe load. The front axle and rear steer-axle pivot form the stability triangle, and the truck and load''s centre of gravity must stay within it.', "order" = 1 WHERE "slug" = 'g-series-counterbalance-forklifts';
--> statement-breakpoint
