UPDATE "families" SET "name" = 'Heavy-Duty Counterbalance Trucks', "summary" = '6–8 t electric counterbalance trucks for heavy pallets, steel, ports and outdoor yards, replacing large diesel trucks without exhaust fumes.', "how_it_works" = 'A **heavy-duty electric counterbalance forklift** does the work of a large diesel truck: steel coils, bagged commodities, beverage pallets in pairs, machinery and container-yard tasks. The layout is the same as a standard counterbalance truck. Forks lift at the front, and the counterweight and battery at the rear keep it balanced. Every major part is scaled up for heavier loads and outdoor duty.

**Power.** These trucks carry large 80 V lithium iron phosphate (LFP) packs. BYD offers 540 or 810 Ah on its 4–5 t trucks and 810 or 1,080 Ah on its 6–8 t trucks, which store far more energy than a light forklift. Two high-power AC traction motors drive the front axle, and a separate AC motor runs the hydraulic pump for lifting, tilting and attachments.

**Brakes and regeneration.** Heavy loads need strong, durable braking. BYD''s 6–8 t trucks use oil-immersed disc brakes, which run sealed in oil and resist dust and water. Regenerative braking on the traction motors puts energy back into the battery whenever the truck slows.

**Mast and tyres.** Masts are heavier-section duplex or triplex designs, and they often carry attachments such as side-shifts, fork positioners or clamps. These trucks usually run on large pneumatic or solid tyres for yards, and BYD notes that its tallest masts on the 6–8 t trucks need widened tyres.

**Charging.** Large packs need high-current chargers. BYD fits 200 A as standard on the 6–8 t trucks, with 400 A fast charging as an option. Planning the charger supply is therefore part of choosing the truck.

**Stability.** Capacity is rated at the load centre shown on the data plate (600 mm for BYD''s 6–8 t trucks). Long or bulky loads, attachments and high lifts all reduce the safe capacity.', "order" = 2 WHERE "slug" = 'heavy-duty-counterbalance-forklifts';
--> statement-breakpoint
