--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "families" SET "name" = 'Towing Tractors', "summary" = 'Battery-electric tugs from 3 t to 25 t towing capacity for moving trains of trailers in factories, ports and logistics hubs.', "how_it_works" = 'An **electric tow tractor** (tug) pulls loads on trailers or carts instead of lifting them. One tractor can move a train of several trailers, so it can replace many forklift trips over long internal routes: between production halls, from warehouse to dispatch, or across port and airport aprons.

**Drawbar pull, not lift.** A tractor is rated by the **towed load** it can pull on level ground. It works by putting traction through its drive wheels, which needs weight on those wheels. Tractors are therefore heavy for their size, and the towing rating drops on slopes and slippery surfaces. A tow coupling at the rear connects the trailers, and a pin or automatic hitch is common.

**Drive.** An AC traction motor drives the wheels through a reduction gearbox and differential, with the speed controlled electronically. When the operator eases off, regenerative braking slows the tractor and train and puts energy back into the battery. Mechanical service and parking brakes hold the train. The larger tractors have hill-hold and slope protection.

**Sizes.** Compact pedestrian or stand-on tugs (around 3–5 t towed) move carts in assembly plants and hospitals. Seated and cab tractors (25 t and above) haul heavy trailer trains outdoors.

**Battery.** BYD''s tractors use lithium iron phosphate (LFP) batteries: 24–48 V on the small tugs and 80 V on the large tractors. Long routes make tractors good candidates for opportunity charging at the end of each loop. The BMS keeps the pack within safe limits.', "order" = 6 WHERE "slug" = 'tow-tractors';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "products" SET "name" = 'QD50', "summary" = 'Compact 5 t electric tow tractor for factory and warehouse cart trains.', "highlights" = '["5,000 kg towing capacity", "48 V 210 Ah LFP battery", "1,580 mm turning radius"]'::jsonb, "specs" = '{"towingCapacity": 5000, "voltage": 48, "batteryCapacity": 210, "turningRadius": 1580, "serviceWeight": 980}'::jsonb, "specs_verified" = true, "order" = 1 WHERE "slug" = 'byd-qd50';
